note SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
note front.om: the ng front end (Hive NG D1b; functions fe_, globals f_), a unit of seed/ng/ng.units after
note ir.om, so it is OM-2 code (om2 reserved words such as at, big, ops are not names here). fe_check takes
note an Omega unit in f_inp (main.om mode @ng front-check) and gives exactly the refusal (stderr line and
note exit code) and the om2 diag/check records that omc gives, but it writes no program: it is the lexer,
note parser and language checks of omc.om @943d9555 (seed/omc/omc.om) with all machine code taken out.
note Made by seed/ng/front/rename.om (rename.map: fe_/f_ names), hand edits that carry an "omc.om ...
note @943d9555 line N" note, and seed/ng/front/prune.om (prune.txt); since then edited here directly.
note Gated by seed/ng/front/gate-front.om against the pinned omc. Not reproduced (D6): error 12 (register
note pool), 14 for trap sites, 24 (branch range). Units it does not take exit 64: x86/EFI targets (D8),
note IR v1 units (first line ir) and run-time pools (global NAME T *, fe_poolstar). An om2 fmt unit gets every
note refusal of omc (fmtprep, then the rest checked
note as OM-2) and no formatted output.
note Notes kept from omc.om still name the AArch64 code omc emits at each check (B.HS trap 3 and so on):
note those are the run-time checks and trap codes the ΩIR emission (IR.md v0.1 s7 chk.* ops, s13) must produce.
note Value slots (fe_alloc, kind 1 values) are omc's pool numbering without its limit; they are the values
note ΩIR builders replace. No heap (decision 24): every input-sized table is a region of the arena of ir.om (ar_m,
note no-caps 2026-11-11), the rest are fixed global pools of language or format size.

note ---- input, output, token ----
global f_inlen ulong 1
global f_irmode ulong 1
global f_cur ulong 1
global f_line ulong 1
global f_tk ulong 1
global f_tw ulong 1
global f_tl ulong 1
global f_ts ulong 1
global f_tbig ulong 1
note f_bc: the byte fe_bskip stopped at
global f_bc ulong 1
note ---- long names (omc.om tok2 and ln_intern, no-caps arena 2026-11-11): fe_tok2 interns each word of
note 9..63 bytes that is not a number as the packed word 1 + 256 * index. Its low byte, 1, is below every
note byte a word can hold (33..255), so it never equals a name of 8 bytes or fewer or a keyword, and two
note words get the same packed word exactly when they are spelled the same: every table that compares packed
note words takes long names unchanged. Arena group long (6): f_ln_o where the spelling starts in the input
note (read there, never copied), f_ln_l its length, f_ln_x the index + 1 before it in its chain; group
note longhash (7): f_ln_h the chained hash, bucket -> index + 1 of the newest, f_lh_b its bits. f_ln_n: the
note count, bounded by the arena only. f_tw8: the word's first 8 bytes before interning (fe_cp_kind reads
note invariant there). Abstract, layout, layout-field and IR-mode names stay at 8.
global f_lh_b ulong 1
global f_ln_n ulong 1
global f_tw8 ulong 1

note ---- OM-2 profile (spec/omegese-om2.md, OMEGESE.md 9.13). om2 is 1 in an OM-2 unit (its first line
note that is not a note or blank is exactly om2, om2 diag or om2 fmt); om2m 0 compile, 1 diag, 2 fmt;
note om2ln/om2pos the line number and offset of that line; fmtm 1 while a unit is formatted; lbase and
note sbase shift reported lines and bytes back to the original input in fmt mode; tka/tkb the byte span of
note the last token; dexp what was being read (0 word 1 value 2 type 3 name 4 number 5 end 6 newline);
note dsev 0 derived, 2 unknown (an undeclared function or struct), 3 error ----
global f_om2 ulong 1
global f_om2m ulong 1
global f_om2ln ulong 1
global f_om2pos ulong 1
global f_chkmod ulong 1
global f_chkln ulong 1
global f_lbase ulong 1
