note lshx: shl (41) or shr (42) on an integer value and an integer or qty amount of another type. omc admits
note only a shift with mixed operand types (rdval's type check skips c 41, 42); a qty amount is a u64 (a qty
note value is error 7 in omc, never here); a bool or float amount, which omc also admits, and a mixed rotate
note (omc error 7) stay not lowered.
fn fe_lshx c ulong a ulong b ulong to bool
if and ne c 41 ne c 42
ret false
end
ret and and ge a 2 le a 9 or and ge b 2 le b 9 eq b 13
end

note lsham: the amount v (integer type b) of a shift of an integer value of type a, as a value of type a.
note omc tests the amount's 64-bit register, sign- or zero-extended by b, against a's width, unsigned
note (bo_schk: CMP Xb, #w; B.HS trap 7), so a negative amount traps 7 like one at or past the width and a
note wide one is never wrapped. Here: conv to u64 (int to int keeps that extension, IR.md s7.3), lt w,
note chk.true 7, then conv to a, exact because the amount is now below w. fe_lbop then checks as before.
fn fe_lsham a ulong b ulong v uint to uint
u = v
if and ne b 5 ne b 13
u = fe_lp1 36 5 0 v
end
k = fe_lp2 32 1 u fe_lcst 5 fe_twid a
fe_lck1 82 7 k
if eq a 5
ret u
end
ret fe_lp1 36 a 0 u
end

note lbop: binary op c (add 33 .. ge 48, rotr 59, rotl 60) on a and b of omc type t, with the checks of
note IR.md s13; a rotate checks its amount like a shift (omc.om rotate: trap 7 at or past the width)
