note lfns: one ΩIR function per unit function, in order (handle = index + 1); main is the export
fn fe_lfns to void
mw = or or or ulong 109 shl ulong 97 8 shl ulong 105 16 shl ulong 110 24
mf = fe_findfn mw 4 0
if eq mf 0
fe_lno
end
if or ne ar_c 22 sub mf 1 0 ne ar_c 21 sub mf 1 8
fe_lno
end
note A `target macos` unit may define `fn libback k ulong a ulong b ulong c ulong d ulong e ulong to ulong`: the
note function library code calls back (a64/DESIGN.md s14). It gets flags bit 1; any other signature is refused.
bf = ulong 0
if eq get f_mac 0 1
bf = fe_findfn 30227092421634412 7 0
end
if ne bf 0
jb = sub bf 1
if or ne ar_c 22 jb 6 ne ar_c 21 jb 5
fe_lno
end
for p ulong 6
q = add mul jb 6 p
if or ne ar_c 35 q 0 ne ar_c 33 q 5
fe_lno
end
end
end
for j ulong get f_nf 0 bound 16777217
k = uint 0
if eq add j 1 mf
k = uint 2
end
fl = uint 0
if eq add j 1 bf
fl = uint 2
end
fe_lfpar j ir_fnew k fl fe_lty ulong uchar get ar_m add get ar_rb 21 j
end
end

note lfpar: the parameters of unit function j (index) on ΩIR function f: a scalar, or a SLICE of an array
note parameter, sized or unsized (access 0 view, 1 edit)
fn fe_lfpar j ulong f uint to void
np = ulong ar_c 22 j
for p ulong np bound 6
q = add mul j 6 p
pk = ar_c 35 q
t = ulong ar_c 33 q
if eq pk 0
v = ir_fpar f fe_lty t
else
if gt pk 3
fe_lno
end
a = uint 0
if eq pk 3
a = uint 1
end
